<!--meta {"lead": "An empty or broken screen is still a screen Maya can use. Each one says what happened, why, and gives one way forward.", "description": "First-run, no-results, error-as-empty and the full error pages, with copy formulas.", "covers": "First-run, no results, error as empty, 404/403/500/offline pages, copy formulas, reference ids"} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Empty and error states use one shape, the <a href="../components/empty-state.html">empty state</a>: an icon in a tinted circle, a title, one sentence, and one primary action (plus at most one secondary). Full-page errors use the same shape inside the normal shell; see <a href="../components/error-page.html">error page</a>. The mocks show 46 of these across appointments, braiders, styles, notifications and the 404, 403, 500 and offline pages.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="when"><h2><a href="#when">When to use which</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Situation</th><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Primary action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Nothing exists yet (no appointments, no notifications)</td><td>First-run, accent icon</td><td>The action that creates the first item: "Explore styles"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Filters or search returned nothing</td><td>No results, search icon, filters stay visible</td><td>"Clear filters"; secondary: widen one filter</td></tr>
      <tr><td>A list or page failed to load</td><td>Error, danger icon (<code>.empty--error</code>)</td><td>"Try again"; secondary: a safe place</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Part of a page failed</td><td>Not an empty state: a warning <a href="../components/alert.html">alert</a> in place of that part</td><td>"Retry reviews"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Wrong address, no permission, server down, offline</td><td><a href="../components/error-page.html">Error page</a> in the shell</td><td>One recovery: "Explore styles", "Sign in", "Try again"</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="structure"><h2><a href="#structure">Structure</a></h2>
  <p>The empty state replaces the list, inside the page shell and under the page header, so navigation and context stay.</p>
  <div class="ds-frame"><div class="ds-frame__body">
    <div class="page-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Appointments</p><p style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">My appointments</p><p class="subtitle">Requests and visits appear here.</p></div></div>
    <section class="empty"><div class="empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:calendar}}</div><h2 class="empty__title">No appointments yet</h2><p class="empty__text">When you request a visit, you’ll find its status and details here.</p><div class="empty__actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Explore styles</a></div></section>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  {{example:[start]First-run, no results and error. Each title is specific to the screen.}}
<div class="card"><section class="empty empty--compact"><div class="empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:bell}}</div><h2 class="empty__title">No updates yet</h2><p class="empty__text">Updates about requests and appointments will appear here.</p><div class="empty__actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Explore styles</a></div></section></div>
<div class="card"><section class="empty empty--compact"><div class="empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:search}}</div><h2 class="empty__title">No braiders match these filters</h2><p class="empty__text">Try a wider price range or distance to see more options.</p><div class="empty__actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Clear filters</button></div></section></div>
<div class="card"><section class="empty empty--compact empty--error"><div class="empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:alert-circle}}</div><h2 class="empty__title">We couldn’t load your appointments</h2><p class="empty__text">Check your connection and try again. Your details are safe.</p><div class="empty__actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Try again</button><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Explore styles</a></div></section></div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Server error with a reference</h3>
  <p>A 500 page gives support something to search for and says what did not happen.</p>
  {{themes}}<section class="empty empty--compact empty--error" style="flex: 1;"><div class="empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:alert-circle}}</div><h2 class="empty__title">HairPop needs a moment</h2><p class="empty__text">We couldn’t load this page. Your booking request has not been resent.</p><div class="empty__actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Try again</button></div><p class="empty__reference">Reference ERR-7F3K2 · Sat 10 Oct, 9:42 am</p></section>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Centred at every width; text is capped at 36ch so lines stay short on desktop.</li>
    <li>Actions wrap and centre on phones; the primary comes first. Error pages add <code>.empty--stack-actions</code>, which stacks the actions at full width below 640px.</li>
    <li>Use <code>.empty--compact</code> inside cards and dialogs, full padding when the state replaces a page’s main content.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The icon is decorative (<code>aria-hidden</code>); the title is a real heading at the next level under the page’s h1.</li>
    <li>When an empty or error state replaces content after a user action (applying filters, retrying), announce it once through the empty state’s own visually hidden <code>role="status"</code> span, written after the state renders ("No braiders match these filters"); use <code>role="alert"</code> only when a retry the person started fails again.</li>
    <li>"Try again" is a button when it retries in place, a link when it reloads the page.</li>
    <li>Error pages keep the skip link, top bar and footer so keyboard users can leave.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Empty text on page|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Accent icon on tint|--color-fg-accent|--color-accent-subtle|3}}
    {{pair:Error icon on tint|--color-danger-icon|--color-danger-bg|3}}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Empty formula:</b> title = "No [things] yet" or what is missing; text = when they will appear or how to get one; action = the verb that makes one.</li>
    <li><b>No-results formula:</b> title names the filter problem; text suggests the one change most likely to help.</li>
    <li><b>Error formula:</b> title "We couldn’t [verb] [thing]"; text says what is safe and what to try; action "Try again".</li>
    <li>Never blame Maya and never say "Oops". Never use the same "Nothing here yet" on every screen.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><section class="empty empty--compact"><h2 class="empty__title">No appointments yet</h2><p class="empty__text">When you request a visit, you’ll find it here.</p></section></div><figcaption>A title that says what is missing on this screen.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><section class="empty empty--compact"><h2 class="empty__title">Nothing here yet</h2><p class="empty__text">There’s no information to show here yet.</p></section></div><figcaption>The same generic title on every screen, as in the mocks.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Try again</button><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Explore styles</a></div><figcaption>One primary recovery and one safe secondary.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><section class="empty empty--compact empty--error"><h2 class="empty__title">HairPop needs a moment</h2><p class="empty__text">We couldn’t load this page.</p></section></div><figcaption>A server error with no reference id and no retry.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/my-appointments/empty|first-run}}
    {{mock:pages/notification-center/empty|first-run}}
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/no-results|no results with filters}}
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/error|error as empty}}
    {{mock:pages/not-found/default|404}}
    {{mock:pages/forbidden/default|403}}
    {{mock:pages/server-error/default|500}}
    {{mock:pages/offline/default|offline}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed: every empty state used "Nothing here yet" and a sparkle (now screen-specific titles and icons); the 500 page had no reference id; empty-state icons were text glyphs ("!", "⌕", "✓") instead of icons.</p>
</section>
